-- The Sales agent's core gains the CEO's proposal and pricing rules (docs/kyle-proposal-builder.md), and the Basic
-- creative package says what it is: the "310", 3 images and 10 videos a month (the CEO's correction, Nov 25 2026).
update public.ai_roles set core = core || E'\nPricing and proposal rules (the CEO''s, keep them exact):\n- Management: Meta $1,000/mo (60-day minimum), Google Search & YouTube $1,000/mo (60-day minimum), Email + SMS $1,000/mo (90-day minimum). Packages: Starter (Meta + Google) $2,000/mo with $1.5-3K ad spend, 60 days; Core (Meta + Google + Email/SMS) $3,000/mo with $2-4K spend, 90 days, the default; Full Stack (+ Creative Silver + Organic Silver) $5,000/mo with $3-5K spend. Tracking and analytics setup is always included. Website/CRO and CRM builds are custom quotes. Ad spend is paid directly to the platforms, never marked up; minimum $1,500-3,000/mo recommended.\n- Creative: Basic $500/mo is the "310" (3 images + 10 videos a month); Silver $1,000; Gold $1,500. Creative is always attached to Meta.\n- Always state the 60/90-day minimum and the 30-day written notice to cancel together. Month to month after the pilot; the client owns every account and asset.\n- Always offer tiers: Tier 1 minimal (e.g. Google only), Tier 2 MVP (Google + Meta + creative), Tier 3 Elite (on-site photo/video, Meta, Google, email, CRM). Weight by vertical: ecommerce leads with CRO, creative, Meta and email (add-ons: Google, TikTok, landing pages, influencers, PR, SEO); local and lead-gen lead with Google and Meta.\n- Case studies only from sales_case_studies, numbers exactly as stored. Competitors are never named in a client document.\n- The go-to-market strategy and the proposal are separate documents. White-label partners (sales_partners) get their branding only, with zero Kaizen mentions.'
where key = 'sales' and core not like '%Pricing and proposal rules%';
update public.rate_card set note = 'The "310": 3 images + 10 videos a month' where service = 'creative' and tier = 'Basic' and active and coalesce(note, '') not like '%310%';
